        "id": 1951687
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-15T17:37:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the chunk you consider is at the bottom of the heap (and is not the last chunk in the heap) you can\u0027t reclaim it.\n\nIf we would destroy it, we wouldn\u0027t have anything to track that VA space (which is now unmapped)\n\nAnother approach would be to have the first chunk being \"static\" and not part of any allocation. I would just be not super keen on making that change now. But happy to discuss this possibility for Android-next (or any upstreaming attempt).",
      "parentUuid": "5df8b6ab_6a2a990f",
